From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raghavt20 <raghavt20@aospa.co>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dolbyui: request BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED

BluetoothUtils$BluetoothProxy.isLowLossnessBTConnected() reflects into
the hidden BluetoothA2dp#getCodecStatus(BluetoothDevice) SystemApi to
detect lossless-codec-capable peripherals (e.g. MotoBuds). That API
requires the caller to hold BLUETOOTH_CONNECT plus either
BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED or an active CompanionDeviceManager association;
the app only requests BLUETOOTH_CONNECT, so on platforms that enforce
this check it throws:

  SecurityException: The application with package name
  com.motorola.dolby.dolbyui does not have a CDM association with the
  Bluetooth Device

repeatedly, crashing the app on every Bluetooth (re)connect. Request
BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED so the app can be allowlisted for it via
privapp-permissions like any other priv-app.

Signed-off-by: raghavt20 <raghavt20@aospa.co>
---
 AndroidManifest.xml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/AndroidManifest.xml b/AndroidManifest.xml
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
     <uses-permission android:name="com.motorola.motobuds.permission.CONNECTION_STATE"/>
     <uses-permission android:maxSdkVersion="30" android:name="android.permission.BLUETOOTH"/>
     <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.BLUETOOTH_CONNECT"/>
+    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED"/>
     <uses-permission android:name="com.motorola.moto.provider.permission.READ_MODES"/>
     <uses-permission android:name="com.motorola.sstservice.permission.MODIFY_AUDIO_SETTINGS"/>
     <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS"/>
